.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_EVENT_ALLOC_HDL 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_event_alloc_hdl ,
.Nm ndi_event_free_hdl ,
.Nm ndi_event_bind_set ,
.Nm ndi_event_unbind_set
.Nd manage nexus event handles and event definitions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_event_alloc_hdl
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "ddi_iblock_cookie_t cookie"
.Fa "ndi_event_hdl_t *ndi_event_hdl"
.Fa "uint_t flag"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_event_free_hdl
.Fa "ndi_event_hdl_t handle"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_event_bind_set
.Fa "ndi_event_hdl_t handle"
.Fa "ndi_event_set_t *ndi_event_set"
.Fa "uint_t flag"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_event_unbind_set
.Fa "ndi_event_hdl_t handle"
.Fa "ndi_event_set_t *ndi_event_set"
.Fa "uint_t flag"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va dip
Nexus node defining the events.
.It Va cookie
Interrupt block cookie used to initialize the event locks.
.It Va ndi_event_hdl
Output pointer receiving the allocated handle.
.It Va handle
Valid event handle returned by allocation.
.It Va ndi_event_set
Event set describing definitions to bind or unbind.
.It Va flag
\fBNDI_SLEEP\fP or \fBNDI_NOSLEEP\fP for allocations; zero for unbinding.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A nexus event handle owns a set of event cookies and their callback
registrations.
\fBndi_event_alloc_hdl()\fP allocates an empty handle for \fBdip\fP and initializes
its locks using the supplied interrupt block cookie.
Pass an appropriate cookie for events delivered at interrupt level, or
\fBNULL\fP for events delivered only from user or kernel context.
\fBNDI_SLEEP\fP allows sleeping allocations; \fBNDI_NOSLEEP\fP requests allocations
that can fail instead of waiting.
.Pp
\fBndi_event_bind_set()\fP adds the definitions in \fBndi_event_set\fP to the handle.
The set must use \fBNDI_EVENTS_REV1\fP.
The event definition array and its name strings are referenced, not copied,
and must remain valid until the corresponding events have been unbound or
the handle has been freed.
Define unique names and tags within the handle.
An already bound event name is skipped.
High-level interrupt events cannot share a handle with kernel or ordinary
interrupt events.
.Pp
\fBndi_event_unbind_set()\fP removes the named definitions from the handle.
The set may describe a subset of previously bound events.
Names that are not bound are ignored.
All callbacks for the selected events must first be removed.
Its \fBflag\fP argument is unused; pass zero.
Both binding and unbinding must be performed while the owning nexus is in
its attach or detach path.
.Pp
\fBndi_event_free_hdl()\fP releases the handle and any remaining event cookies.
All callback registrations must already have been removed, and the caller
must prevent concurrent users of the handle.
The handle and all of its cookies are invalid afterwards.
It does not free the caller's event definition array or strings.
.Sh CONTEXT
Allocate and free handles from user or kernel context.
Binding and unbinding are restricted to the owning nexus
\fBattach(9E)\fP or \fBdetach(9E)\fP path.
\fBNDI_NOSLEEP\fP does not relax the attach/detach restriction.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Allocation and binding return \fBNDI_SUCCESS\fP or \fBNDI_FAILURE\fP.
Binding can fail for an invalid version, incompatible event levels,
incorrect calling context, or insufficient memory.
Unbinding returns \fBNDI_SUCCESS\fP, or \fBNDI_FAILURE\fP for an invalid version,
incorrect calling context, or outstanding callbacks.
Outstanding callbacks violate the calling contract and can also trigger an
assertion in a debug kernel.
Freeing a valid, unused handle returns \fBNDI_SUCCESS\fP.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr attach 9E ,
.Xr detach 9E ,
.Xr ndi_event_add_callback 9F ,
.Xr ndi_event_retrieve_cookie 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F ,
.Xr ndi_event_definition 9S ,
.Xr ndi_event_set 9S
